  "difficulty_reason": "Beyond ordinary finite-dimensional module and lattice preliminaries, the proof classifies arbitrary torsion covers by minimal extending modules and bricks and establishes their dual co-extension criterion. It constructs a lower cover for each member of a hom-orthogonal brick family, then proves irredundancy and unique lowest refinement of the corresponding join representation in the possibly infinite torsion lattice. The resulting global canonical-join/brick-complex equivalence is beyond ordinary doctoral algebra qualifiers.",
